{"id":"mahabharata-7-112","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":112,"title":"द्वादशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 112 · Bhima kills ten Kaurava heroes","summary":{"en":"Karna rushes at Bhima like a rutting elephant, but Bhima kills ten Kaurava heroes while Karna looks on. Karna weeps, and tells Duryodhana of his heavy cost.","kn":"ಮದಗಜದಂತೆ ಕರ್ಣ ಭೀಮನ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ಕರ್ಣನ ಕಣ್ಣೆದುರೇ ಭೀಮ ಹತ್ತು ಕೌರವ ವೀರರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಣ ದುಃಖಿಸಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಈ ಭಾರೀ ನಷ್ಟ ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कर्ण मतवाले हाथी की तरह भीम पर झपटता है, पर कर्ण के देखते-देखते भीम दस कौरव वीरों को मार देते हैं। कर्ण दुखी होता है और दुर्योधन से इस भारी क्षति की बात कहता है।","te":"కర్ణుడు మదగజంలా భీమునిపై దూకుతాడు, కానీ కర్ణుని కళ్లెదుటే భీముడు పది మంది కౌరవ వీరులను చంపుతాడు. కర్ణుడు దుఃఖించి ఈ భారీ నష్టాన్ని దుర్యోధనునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மதயானை போல் கர்ணன் பீமனைத் தாக்க, ஆனால் கர்ணன் பார்க்கையிலேயே பீமன் பத்துக் கௌரவ வீரரைக் கொல்கிறான். கர்ணன் வருந்தி இப்பெரும் இழப்பைத் துரியோதனனிடம் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"കർണ്ണൻ മദയാനയെപ്പോലെ ഭീമന്റെ നേർക്ക് പാഞ്ഞടുക്കുന്നു; എന്നാൽ കർണ്ണൻ നോക്കിനിൽക്കെ ഭീമൻ പത്ത് കൗരവ വീരന്മാരെ വധിക്കുന്നു. കർണ്ണൻ കരഞ്ഞുകൊണ്ട് തന്റെ ഭാരിച്ച നഷ്ടം ദുര്യോധനനെ അറിയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.112; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भीमसेनस्य राधेयः श्रुत्वा ज्यातलनिस्वनम् ।\nनामृष्यत यथा मत्तो गजः प्रतिगजस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the twang and slap of Bhimasena's bowstring, Radheya could not bear it, as a rutting elephant cannot bear the trumpet of a rival elephant."}},{"n":2,"text":"अपक्रम्य स भीमस्य मुहूर्तं शरगोचरात् ।\nतव चाधिरथिर्दृष्ट्वा स्यन्दनेभ्यश्च्युतान्सुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Withdrawing for a moment from Bhima's arrow range, and seeing your sons fallen from their chariots, Adhiratha's son,"}},{"n":3,"text":"भीमसेनेन निहतान्विमना दुःखितोऽभवत् ।\nनिःश्वसन्दीर्घमुष्णं च पुनः पाण्डवमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"dejected and sad that they had been slain by Bhimasena, sighing long and hot, again went against the Pandava."}},{"n":4,"text":"स ताम्रनयनः क्रोधाच्छ्वसन्निव महोरगः ।\nबभौ कर्णः शरानस्यन्रश्मिवानिव भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His eyes copper-red with anger, hissing like a great serpent, Karna shone, shooting arrows like the sun with its rays."}},{"n":5,"text":"रश्मिजालैरिवार्कस्य विततैर्भरतर्षभ ।\nकर्णचापच्युतैर्बाणैः प्राच्छाद्यत वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrikodara was covered, best of Bharatas, with arrows loosed from Karna's bow, like a spread net of the sun's rays."}},{"n":6,"text":"कर्णचापच्युताश्चित्राः शरा बर्हिणवाससः ।\nविविशुः सर्वतः पार्थं वासायेवाण्डजा द्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those varied arrows with peacock feathers, loosed from Karna's bow, entered Partha on all sides like birds entering a tree for their nest."}},{"n":7,"text":"कर्णचापच्युता बाणाः संपतन्तस्ततस्ततः ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खा व्यराजन्त हंसाः श्रेणीकृता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrows loosed from Karna's bow, falling here and there, with gold feathers, shone like swans in a row."}},{"n":8,"text":"चापध्वजोपस्करेभ्यश्छत्रादीषामुखाद्युगात् ।\nप्रभवन्तो व्यदृश्यन्त राजन्नाधिरथेः शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrows of Adhiratha's son were seen coming forth, O king, from his bow, banner and gear, from the umbrella, the pole's end and the yoke."}},{"n":9,"text":"खं पूरयन्महावेगान्खगमान्खगवाससः ।\nसुवर्णविकृतांश्चित्रान्मुमोचाधिरथिः शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Adhiratha's son loosed arrows that filled the sky, very swift, flying, with bird-feather vanes, gold-wrought and varied."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमन्तकमिवायस्तमापतन्तं वृकोदरः ।\nत्यक्त्वा प्राणानभिक्रुध्य विव्याध नवभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he came at him like Death, taking pains, Vrikodara, giving up his life, enraged, struck him with nine arrows."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्य वेगमसंसह्यं दृष्ट्वा कर्णस्य पाण्डवः ।\nमहतश्च शरौघांस्तान्नैवाव्यथत वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the unbearable speed of Karna and those great floods of arrows, the valiant Pandava did not waver."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो विधम्याधिरथेः शरजालानि पाण्डवः ।\nविव्याध कर्णं विंशत्या पुनरन्यैः शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava, destroying Adhiratha's son's nets of arrows, struck Karna with twenty and again with other sharp arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथैव हि शरैः पार्थः सूतपुत्रेण छादितः ।\nतथैव कर्णं समरे छादयामास पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Partha was covered with arrows by the charioteer's son, so the Pandava covered Karna in the battle."}},{"n":14,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु भीमसेनस्य विक्रमं युधि भारत ।\nअभ्यनन्दंस्त्वदीयाश्च संप्रहृष्टाश्च चारणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhimasena's prowess in the fight, O Bharata, your own men and the delighted charanas applauded."}},{"n":15,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः कृपो द्रौणिर्मद्रराजो जयद्रथः ।\nउत्तमौजा युधामन्युः सात्यकिः केशवार्जुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Kripa, Drona's son, the king of Madra, Jayadratha, Uttamaujas, Yudhamanyu, Satyaki, and Keshava and Arjuna,"}},{"n":16,"text":"कुरुपाण्डवानां प्रवरा दश राजन्महारथाः ।\nसाधु साध्विति वेगेन सिंहनादमथानदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"those ten great chariot-warriors, best of the Kurus and the Pandavas, O king, cried \"Well done, well done!\" and roared lion's roars with force."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु तुमुले शब्दे प्रवृत्ते लोमहर्षणे ।\nअभ्यभाषत पुत्रांस्ते राजन्दुर्योधनस्त्वरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that hair-raising, tumultuous noise went on, Duryodhana hastily spoke to your sons."}},{"n":18,"text":"राज्ञश्च राजपुत्रांश्च सोदर्यांश्च विशेषतः ।\nकर्णं गच्छत भद्रं वः परीप्सन्तो वृकोदरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go, to Karna, you kings and princes, especially my brothers, good fortune to you, protecting him from Vrikodara.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"पुरा निघ्नन्ति राधेयं भीमचापच्युताः शराः ।\nते यतध्वं महेष्वासाः सूतपुत्रस्य रक्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The arrows shot from Bhima's bow will soon kill Radheya. So strive, great archers, to protect the charioteer's son.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"दुर्योधनसमादिष्टाः सोदर्याः सप्त मारिष ।\nभीमसेनमभिद्रुत्य संरब्धाः पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Commanded by Duryodhana, seven brothers, sir, rushed at Bhimasena in fury and surrounded him."}},{"n":21,"text":"ते समासाद्य कौन्तेयमावृण्वञ्शरवृष्टिभिः ।\nपर्वतं वारिधाराभिः प्रावृषीव बलाहकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the son of Kunti, they covered him with showers of arrows, as clouds cover a mountain with streams of water in the rainy season."}},{"n":22,"text":"तेऽपीडयन्भीमसेनं क्रुद्धाः सप्त महारथाः ।\nप्रजासंहरणे राजन्सोमं सप्त ग्रहा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those seven great chariot-warriors, angry, tormented Bhimasena, O king, as the seven planets torment the moon at the world's dissolution."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो वामेन कौन्तेयः पीडयित्वा शरासनम् ।\nमुष्टिना पाण्डवो राजन्दृढेन सुपरिष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Kunti, the Pandava, pressing his bow with his left hand and holding it firmly in his fist, O king,"}},{"n":24,"text":"मनुष्यसमतां ज्ञात्वा सप्त संधाय सायकान् ।\nतेभ्यो व्यसृजदायस्तः सूर्यरश्मिनिभान्प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"knowing the foe as only human, set seven arrows and loosed them at them with effort, the lord, shining like the sun's rays."}},{"n":25,"text":"निरस्यन्निव देहेभ्यस्तनयानामसूंस्तव ।\nभीमसेनो महाराज पूर्ववैरमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, remembering the old enmity, as if driving the lives of your sons out of their bodies, great king,"}},{"n":26,"text":"ते क्षिप्ता भीमसेनेन शरा भारत भारतान् ।\nविदार्य खं समुत्पेतुः स्वर्णपुङ्खाः शिलाशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those arrows sent by Bhimasena, O Bharata, tore through the Bharatas and flew up into the sky, gold-feathered and whetted on stone."}},{"n":27,"text":"तेषां विदार्य चेतांसि शरा हेमविभूषिताः ।\nव्यराजन्त महाराज सुपर्णा इव खेचराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced their minds, those arrows adorned with gold shone, great king, like Garuda-birds flying in the sky."}},{"n":28,"text":"शोणितादिग्धवाजाग्राः सप्त हेमपरिष्कृताः ।\nपुत्राणां तव राजेन्द्र पीत्वा शोणितमुद्गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The seven arrows, their tips stained with blood and decked with gold, rose up, king of kings, having drunk the blood of your sons."}},{"n":29,"text":"ते शरैर्भिन्नमर्माणो रथेभ्यः प्रापतन्क्षितौ ।\nगिरिसानुरुहा भग्ना द्विपेनेव महाद्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their vital parts broken by the arrows, they fell from their chariots to the ground, like great trees growing on a mountain slope, broken by an elephant."}},{"n":30,"text":"शत्रुंजयः शत्रुसहश्चित्रश्चित्रायुधो दृढः ।\nचित्रसेनो विकर्णश्च सप्तैते विनिपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shatrunjaya, Shatrusaha, Chitra, Chitrayudha, Dridha, Chitrasena and Vikarna, these seven were struck down."}},{"n":31,"text":"तान्निहत्य महाबाहू राधेयस्यैव पश्यतः ।\nसिंहनादरवं घोरमसृजत्पाण्डुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed them in front of Radheya himself, the mighty-armed son of Pandu gave a terrible lion's roar."}},{"n":32,"text":"स रवस्तस्य शूरस्य धर्मराजस्य भारत ।\nआचख्याविव तद्युद्धं विजयं चात्मनो महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That roar of the hero, O Bharata, seemed to tell the king of dharma of that fight and of his own great victory."}},{"n":33,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा सुमहानादं भीमसेनस्य धन्विनः ।\nबभूव परमा प्रीतिर्धर्मराजस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that very great cry of the archer Bhimasena, the king of dharma felt the highest joy in the battle."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततो हृष्टो महाराज वादित्राणां महास्वनैः ।\nभीमसेनरवं पार्थः प्रतिजग्राह सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, delighted, great king, with the great sound of instruments, Partha answered Bhimasena's roar from every side."}},{"n":35,"text":"अभ्ययाच्चैव समरे द्रोणमस्त्रभृतां वरम् ।\nहर्षेण महता युक्तः कृतसंज्ञे वृकोदरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And having received the agreed sign from Vrikodara, he went with great joy against Drona, best of those who bear weapons."}},{"n":36,"text":"एकत्रिंशन्महाराज पुत्रांस्तव महारथान् ।\nहतान्दुर्योधनो दृष्ट्वा क्षत्तुः सस्मार तद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing thirty-one of your sons, great chariot-warriors, slain, great king, Duryodhana remembered the words of Kshatta."}},{"n":37,"text":"तदिदं समनुप्राप्तं क्षत्तुर्हितकरं वचः ।\nइति संचिन्त्य राजासौ नोत्तरं प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here has come to pass that advice of Kshatta, which served my good,\" thinking so, the king gave no answer."}},{"n":38,"text":"यद्द्यूतकाले दुर्बुद्धिरब्रवीत्तनयस्तव ।\nयच्च कर्णोऽब्रवीत्कृष्णां सभायां परुषं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What your evil-minded son said at the time of the dice game, and the harsh word Karna spoke to Krishna in the assembly,"}},{"n":39,"text":"प्रमुखे पाण्डुपुत्राणां तव चैव विशां पते ।\nकौरवाणां च सर्वेषामाचार्यस्य च संनिधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"in the presence of the sons of Pandu and of you, lord of the people, and of all the Kauravas, in the presence of the teacher:"}},{"n":40,"text":"विनष्टाः पाण्डवाः कृष्णे शाश्वतं नरकं गताः ।\nपतिमन्यं वृणीष्वेति तस्येदं फलमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, the Pandavas are ruined and gone to an eternal hell; choose another husband.\" The fruit of that has now arrived."}},{"n":41,"text":"यत्स्म तां परुषाण्याहुः सभामानाय्य द्रौपदीम् ।\nपाण्डवानुग्रधनुषः क्रोधयन्तस्तवात्मजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because your sons spoke those harsh words when Draupadi was brought to the assembly, angering the Pandavas, fierce archers,"}},{"n":42,"text":"तं भीमसेनः क्रोधाग्निं त्रयोदश समाः स्थितम् ।\nविसृजंस्तव पुत्राणामन्तं गच्छति कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, releasing that fire of anger that stood for thirteen years, is going toward the end of your sons, Kaurava."}},{"n":43,"text":"विलपंश्च बहु क्षत्ता शमं नालभत त्वयि ।\nसपुत्रो भरतश्रेष्ठ तस्य भुङ्क्ष्व फलोदयम् ।\nहतो विकर्णो राजेन्द्र चित्रसेनश्च वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Kshatta lamented much, he got no peace from you. Now, best of Bharatas, enjoy the rise of its fruit together with your sons. Vikarna is dead, king of kings, and the brave Chitrasena."}},{"n":44,"text":"प्रवरानात्मजानां ते सुतांश्चान्यान्महारथान् ।\nयान्यांश्च ददृशे भीमश्चक्षुर्विषयमागतान् ।\nपुत्रांस्तव महाबाहो त्वरया ताञ्जघान ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the best of your sons, and other great chariot-warriors, whomever Bhima saw come within his sight, mighty-armed, he swiftly struck down your sons."}},{"n":45,"text":"त्वत्कृते ह्यहमद्राक्षं दह्यमानां वरूथिनीम् ।\nसहस्रशः शरैर्मुक्तैः पाण्डवेन वृषेण च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of you I saw the host burning, with thousands of arrows loosed by the Pandava and by Vrisha."}}]}]}